  "title": "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.68",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "A finite group $G$ is said to be semi-abelian if it has a sequence of subgroups $1=G_0\\leqslant G_1\\leqslant\\cdots\\leqslant G_n=G$ such that for every $i$ the subgroup $G_{i+1}$ is isomorphic to a quotient of a semidirect product $A_i\\rtimes G_i$ for some abelian group $A_i$.\n\nConjecture: Semi-abelian finite groups are monomial.",
